# Real, previously-undiscovered bug found in Phase 6 (ROADMAP.md): without
# this file, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile's `build` stage pulls in whatever
# happens to be on the host running `docker build` — most importantly a
# host-local `node_modules`, which clobbers the `deps` stage's own
# carefully-installed one (built for the container's platform/pnpm layout,
# not the host's) and breaks the later `COPY --from=build
# /app/node_modules/.prisma` step in a way that only reproduces when the
# host happens to already have `node_modules` present — invisible in CI
# (a clean checkout has none) but real for any local `docker build`.

# Dependencies (deps/prod-deps stages install these fresh, per-platform)
node_modules/

# Build output (the build stage produces its own)
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment — real secrets must never enter a build context/image layer;
# docker-compose.yml injects .env via `env_file` at container *runtime*
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control / CI / editor — irrelevant to the image, and .git in
# particular can be large and changes on every commit, busting layer cache
.git/
.github/

# Testing / coverage
coverage/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Local dispute evidence storage (EVIDENCE_STORAGE_DIR default) — runtime
# data, never something to bake into an image
storage/evidence/

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
